In my last game I made an observation that first puzzled me. Reading a
scroll of create monster in the Caveman's quest sent in four titans, and
those titans quite immediately summoned six black dragons in one turn.
The reason for the titans, it seems, was that I've genocided all 'h' and
all 'H', and titans are exempt from class geno 'H'. The Caveman's quest
monsters are typically bugbears and giants, or random 'h' and random 'H',
but in the Home 1 level, where I was, only bugbears are defined. I wonder
whether the monster definition of the "fill" levels are also taken into
account for random monster generation; that would at least explain that
horde of titans.

